{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves","id":850497,"title":"[2e] Feeding on Werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-21T04:54:46-07:00","id":850497,"title":"[2e] Feeding on Werewolves","content":"Hey all, <br /> <br /> I'm in the process of arranging a 2e game, and one of the characters I'd like to have running around in the backstory (Probably dead by the time the game starts) is a vampire who feeds on Werewolves. There's some more backstory to it, but the gist is that the vampires drove the werewolves out of their city, but new ones keep popping up. One of the elders of the area makes it his job to hunt down future Werewolves as they approach the first change, and drives them to it by tormenting them subtly. Then he eats them. <br /> <br /> But before I introduce it into the game, I want to make sure it's something that works by the mechanics. Will a Nosferatu with a decent level of Vigor be able to overcome the ludicrous regeneration of even a brand new Gauru-form Werewolf? Is Blood Potency 5 or 6, 3 to 4 points of Vigor and a decent Brawl skill enough to do it? Turns out, not really. <br /> <br /> Rough maths I'm using here is 4 points of Strength, 4 points of Vigor, 4 points of Brawl (I.e. Leaving some room around the top end, especially for BP 6), a +2 Brawl specialty, giving 14 dice (~5 successes), compared to an average Gauru (2 base strength + 3 for Gauru, 2 Brawl) of 7 dice (&gt;2 successes). The Vampire will regularly win, but he'll not manage an exceptional success often. And when he wins he'll do ~5 successes of damage +0L for fangs +4 for Vigor, for 9 levels of damage. But not enough to deal even a single point of Aggravated damage (Average Gauru has 11 health boxes), meaning that next turn the Werewolf heals fully. And he only needs to win the roll once to break free.<br /> <br /> Options I'm considering are Professional Training (Which feels a bit weak. Professional Werewolf hunter? Professional wrestler? Lot of work to justify either, I think), having his fangs silvered (which instantly turns the maths from an endless struggle to a two turn kill), or something clever that I've not yet found. I'd prefer something clever, as I'm not sure that relying on silver gives the character the bad-ass feel that I was going for. Then again, maybe he could hide the fact, which suddenly makes him appear both more bad-ass and (when discovered) makes him appear more cunning. <br /> <br /> Nosferatu isn't set in stone. If another Clan works better, suggest away. It's just where I started, for the monster who scares other monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T05:13:55-07:00","id":850506,"title":"","content":"Well...if the BP of the vampire is 5 - 6....you can use 5 - 6 vitae at turn. Save 2 or 3 for the physical disciplines, (resilence, Vigor and celerity if him have them) and use the rest to rise strenght (3 vitae in strenght are 6 more dots on the attack pool).<br /> Furthemore, Nosferatu could use cloack of shadow and deal a surprise attack dealing Killing Blow. With this you don't need to roll your dice pool. Every dice is a success for the attack. So you deal (with your examples) 18 damage plus weapon plus 4 for active vigor.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Remember that the Nosferatu can go invisible every turn of the combat and repeat the same strategy.<br /> If the vampire is going out of vitae, use a grappling move to drink a little bit. (I suppose that a Vampire used to feed from werewolves have the Unnatural affinity merit in order to gain Vitae drinking their blood).<br /> Anyway I suppose that a Gangrel with Unholy CLaw (that deal aggravate damage) or a Daeva (both with obfuscate is better), could works better.<br /> <br /> And go with Ride the Wave that adds to your dice pool 5-6 more dice from your BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-21-2016, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T05:41:26-07:00","id":850513,"title":"","content":"Also, in grapple, with an exceptional success you use two moves. One is a damage move, one is a feed move; so with 5 sux, that is 5 damage (Damage move), + (Up to BP) damage from blood loss (feed move).<br /> <br /> This assumes a) blood loss harms wolves like mortals, and b) werewolves regenerate their blood every turn. If these are both the case, a grappling vampire has at least a diceroll advantage a lot of the time; adding X from frenzy and up to 2X from blood expenditure, and can refresh this every time he wins with the feed move. Wrestling a Gauru wolf becomes a war of attrition; if the vampire can field the damage, the constant supply of blood in a regenerating gauru can add a lot of dice. <br /> <br /> A gauru will still win if he breaks the grapple and goes for bites; but a grappling vampire, who uses feed move and damage move the same turn with an exceptional success, is a deadly thing - particularly with the never-ending blood-supply of a regenerating werewolf (if this is the case).<br /> <br /> Of course, you could use silver sniper bullets instead...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T05:56:28-07:00","id":850515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=850506#post850506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthemore, Nosferatu could use cloack of shadow and deal a surprise attack dealing Killing Blow. With this you don't need to roll your dice pool. Every dice is a success for the attack. So you deal (with your examples) 18 damage plus weapon plus 4 for active vigor.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSurprise attacks don't usually allow Killing Blow mechanics; they just reduce the target's Defence to 0.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T06:01:11-07:00","id":850517,"title":"","content":"During frenzy or ride rhe wave you can grapple and bite (and drink up to BP vitae) in the same turn. P.104.<br /> Anyway the best choice should be go with obfuscate and killing blow. Even without weapon, in your example, you will deal 27 DAMAGES (not dice) each turn. (Defense doesn't apply flagainst a surprise attack).<br /> If you use also unholy claw this damage is aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T06:10:15-07:00","id":850523,"title":"","content":"Acro is right here; also note that a surprise attack is not guaranteed with Obfuscate - it will need a roll, the vamps dex+stel+obfuscate vs. the wolfs wits+comp+perception bonus. No means a simple thing. If riding the wave, the frenzy bonus can help the vamp.<br /> <br /> This will no doubt lead to retribution from wolves - a siskur dah - if any survive to tell the tale. But as the setting of a story, it is rich with subplot.<br /> <br /> I think the main problem is fielding the damage from the wolf. It gets one or two bites in, the vampire is a sandwich. So Fortitude is necessary if this is a regular technique; animalism also helps (a couple of zombie dogs can really help hold someone down for the grapple). Protean claws for agg too? There may be a reason Gangrel survive so well in the wilds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T06:45:34-07:00","id":850528,"title":"","content":"Probably I missed something. I known that in first ed. to deal a killing blow you needed the murder kill merit, while in second edition this merit doesen't exists anymore. The vampire core book simply say that, if you have time and the victim can't defend you can deal a killing blow.<br /> If not, how can a vampire deal a killing blow?<br /> Anyway I think is weird that an invisible attacker, with no smell an no sound (obfuscate), take just a few dice bonus for a surprise attack. In order to track an obfuscate subject the pursuer need to achieves an amount of successes in an EXTENDED roll on wits+composure-obfuscate, equal to the vampires wits+stealth+obfuscate. Here an extended roll and for an attack a single roll? Anyway it's ok but explain me the killing blow mechanics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-21-2016, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T07:42:56-07:00","id":850545,"title":"","content":"The notion that a vampire could somehow scrutinize a whole city for signs of the First Change without spiritual insights or prophecies is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way? Why isn't the elder just killing the Nuzusul before the change? How did vampires drove the Uratha out of the city when they could have exiled themselves into the shadow, surveyed Havens and set them ablaze with spontaneous use of Influence: Fire from the safety of the Gauntlet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:03:37-07:00","id":850556,"title":"","content":"One has to be immobilized or incapacitated. An unconscious or fully restrained person can be subject to a killing blow.<br /> <br /> There is a werewolf/beast merit that allows a killing blow on targets without their defense. Though for werewolves at least, it requires the Garou form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:13:12-07:00","id":850560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=850545#post850545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The notion that a vampire could somehow scrutinize a whole city for signs of the First Change without spiritual insights or prophecies is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way? Why isn't the elder just killing the Nuzusul before the change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, tracking down First Changes seems on the easy side of the weirder things you can do with all of time and a good amount of connections. <br /> <br /> The First Change isn't subtle. There's days to weeks of weird things happening, some of which are easily visible to others. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Squirrels and rabbits literally flee screaming in fear, while strange dogs saunter alongside her on the street, ignoring their masters\u2019 commands. Time and space lurch. She walks for five minutes and travels five miles, or she finds herself in horrible nightmare-spaces like eternal hallways or burning buildings with no exit. In the middle of the afternoon. For no reason. </div> </div> </div>A decent network of connections and some crooked doctors reporting people reporting psych symptoms and that seems easy enough. You're not going to find all of them, but you will find some. <br /> <br /> As for why, because he can. It's about making a statement and having a hobby. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How did vampires drove the Uratha out of the city when they could have exiled themselves into the shadow, surveyed Havens and set them ablaze with spontaneous use of Influence: Fire from the safety of the Gauntlet? </div> </div> </div>That's a good question. The easy answer is because that's what the story calls for. I'm trying to set up a fallen vampire utopia (&quot;Back in our day the werewolves were under control, humanity knew it's place and we had all of the blood we wanted&quot;). Part of that is that in the past it had to actually be better. <br /> <br /> Perhaps working from an Oubliette hidden from the Shadow to deliver a massive first strike which eliminated the majority of werewolves. Or maybe they did it with just political power - There's plenty of ways that werewolves could be pushed out by humanity with only a little coaxing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:22:25-07:00","id":850563,"title":"","content":"You know vampires and werewolves aren't enemies, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:27:26-07:00","id":850566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=850563#post850563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know vampires and werewolves aren't enemies, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither are humans and deer, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:33:36-07:00","id":850573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=850563#post850563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know vampires and werewolves aren't enemies, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditionally, no. But again, for the backstory I'm establishing, they are. The city was completely dominated by vampires in the past, both the public, political aspects, and the supernatural. And now (~150 years later) it's <i>not</i>. The vampires are vulnerable. They don't have deep political power, or hold their territory uncontested. They have enemies because of how they acted when they had power. <br /> <br /> I think Ephsy had the right answer in prophecy, thinking about it. A Crone has tools for tracking down a baby werewolf (Although not published yet in 2nd ed), as well as Feeding the Crone, which would make murdering a Garou-form wolf pretty easy, at the cost of not feeding. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:37:25-07:00","id":850575,"title":"","content":"It's Gauru. Garou is from the entirely unrelated Werewolf the Apocalypse game.<br /> <br /> You should note that if this vampire can predict the thing that, by book, cannot be predicted, she would be a target for many, many werewolves. The Pure would love to be able to have access to werewolves who haven't changed. People can be wolf-blooded for seconds or decades or from birth before their First Change, but getting access to them before they make that change would be a real win for the Pure, or really any faction that wants to groom werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:44:29-07:00","id":850580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=850575#post850575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Gauru. Garou is from the entirely unrelated Werewolf the Apocalypse game.<br /> <br /> You should note that if this vampire can predict the thing that, by book, cannot be predicted, she would be a target for many, many werewolves. The Pure would love to be able to have access to werewolves who haven't changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah, so it is. No idea how I managed that considering it's right in every other post and I've not played WtA. <br /> <br /> And I hadn't really thought about predicting it much before it happened, so much as during the period of the change. <br /> <br /> Historically (Read: 1st ed WtF) Werewolves tended to spot them during this period on their own. I've got no idea if that's been dropped in 2nd ed, or just de-emphasised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:51:28-07:00","id":850590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=850580#post850580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Historically (Read: 1st ed WtF) Werewolves tended to spot them during this period on their own. I've got no idea if that's been dropped in 2nd ed, or just de-emphasised.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're playing in first edition, you'll have a much easier time eating werewolves, but even then it wasn't a guarantee.<br /> <br /> A gangrel would probably work better, especially if they had their Protean at 5 dots. At that point the battle doesn't become trading blow-for-blow. It's also worth noting that if your vampire specializes in hunting werewolves, a silver bullet from long range is going to be vastly superior, and safer method to do it. If you really want to go all the way, the vampire can simply have a dominated and blood bound werewolf who was 'his' from the First Change. Being kept from the sacred hunt means he would be low enough on Essence to never really use most of his werewolf powers, he wouldn't be part of a tribe and have training, and even changing would be hard for him. Except death rage, which he would probably do very easily, and under a trigger easily available to a vampire who had studied him long enough. Gauru and vampire versus gauru is a much easier fight. Obviously if you go this way, a vampire with Dominate would be best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-21-2016, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:27:01-07:00","id":850613,"title":"","content":"So, I have a couple of options for solution (realizing I don't know anything about new werewolf beyond what you've said in the thread above):<br /> <br /> 1) Police Tactics 3 to speed-cuff with Silver restraints of some kind, especially using grappling 3 (joint lock) as the lead in for more damage<br /> <br /> 2) A devotion that prevents wounds from healing--maybe something like Nightmare/Vigor? Spend something to make the wounds <i>horrific</i> and thus unable to close for some short period of time. It would basically only be useful against supernaturals, but it would be very useful against them. <br /> <br /> 3) A devotion that prevents or reverses transformation, again, Nightmare/Vigor, maybe? It can lock you into a specific form or force you into your natural form? I don't know, just brainstorming<br /> <br /> Option 2 and 3 would also work as Cruac rituals, probably. I don't know, do werewolves really just regen fully every round? Or is that a function only of their Crinos/Garou form? Does it still have a time limit like in 1e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:27:19-07:00","id":850614,"title":"","content":"Here's my question - why are we assuming mid-Death Rage feeding? Nosferatu can be skilled enough to go Obfuscated if things get too hairy, then poof back when the Gauru form wears out. A better question might be this - what happens when the werewolf simply goes Urhan and runs away? Given the chase rules, there's not a ghost of a chance that a vampire can catch one. Even with Celerity. Irraka stalker pulls their own hiding moves? Clash of Wills with rote quality on the werewolf's part means that the vampire likely loses here as well.<br /> <br /> There's lots of ways this can play out, but I feel like we're assuming werewolves are going to be mindlessly Death Raging as their only tactic. And even then, many werewolves have less rage in them than others, and aren't combatants, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:48:01-07:00","id":850673,"title":"","content":"Yes Protean 5 ia another good point (unless fire access). You could make your firsts damage (possibly aggrvated), become a cloud of mist, heal up and drink from his wounds and, full of blood, start again.<br /> Obfuscate it's another good point. Disappear, heal up, and surprise attack again. <br /> The best (physical) way is always deal aggravated damages with unholy or feeding the crone. A BP 6 vampire, riding the wave, with vigor and rising strenght with vitae, should have a very big dice pool.<br /> Using in a smart way dominate or Majesty is another good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T12:32:55-07:00","id":857243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=850614#post850614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my question - why are we assuming mid-Death Rage feeding?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, because I had a scene in my head and I wanted to see if it was mechanically supported. It wasn't really anything more than that.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=850563#post850563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know vampires and werewolves aren't enemies, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I've already replied to this once, but I've been thinking about it and I'm not sure it's true in 2nd ed. Even if they're not explicitly enemies, I think they're going to be in conflict more often than not. <br /> <br /> My understanding of their relationship in 1st ed is that they've got very little cross-over. Vampires want to feed, and they want power. Werewolves want to hunt spirits and maintain the balance. They have no reason to attack each other, and can basically co-exist without ever noticing each other (Outside of a particularly dumb vampire accidentally trying to eat a werewolf, or a vampire working with spirits). <br /> <br /> With the greater variety within the pack, 2nd ed Werewolf drastically increases the amount of non-werewolves that your average werewolf cares for. You've got the wolfblooded, you've got the human members of the pack, and you've got all of their friends and family. Each of those is a viable target for your average vampire, but if they get snacked on, the pack is probably going to react. That's about as visceral a breach of a werewolf's territory as you're going to get - One of <i>their</i> people has been targeted by a vampire.<br /> <br /> From the vampires point of view, there's no real easy way to differentiate these from their regular prey. And I think few vampires would be willing to constrain their feeding to avoid someone who <i>might</i> be related to a werewolf pack. Placing further restrictions within their feeding grounds is a big deal. <br /> <br /> With sufficient numbers of each, conflict seems pretty inevitable. And avoiding it seems like a lot of sacrifice that neither side will be willing to make. If they're balanced in power, I think you'll see a lot of conflict. If the werewolves are dominant, I'd expect to see more vampires within packs and the freelancers being very careful about who they feed on. If the vampires are dominant, they're going to feed on whoever they want. I don't know if the werewolves have a good reaction to that short of escalating to outright war. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:12:15-07:00","id":857280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=857243#post857243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, because I had a scene in my head and I wanted to see if it was mechanically supported. It wasn't really anything more than that.I know I've already replied to this once, but I've been thinking about it and I'm not sure it's true in 2nd ed. Even if they're not explicitly enemies, I think they're going to be in conflict more often than not.<br /> <br /> My understanding of their relationship in 1st ed is that they've got very little cross-over. Vampires want to feed, and they want power. Werewolves want to hunt spirits and maintain the balance. They have no reason to attack each other, and can basically co-exist without ever noticing each other (Outside of a particularly dumb vampire accidentally trying to eat a werewolf, or a vampire working with spirits).<br /> <br /> With the greater variety within the pack, 2nd ed Werewolf drastically increases the amount of non-werewolves that your average werewolf cares for. You've got the wolfblooded, you've got the human members of the pack, and you've got all of their friends and family. Each of those is a viable target for your average vampire, but if they get snacked on, the pack is probably going to react. That's about as visceral a breach of a werewolf's territory as you're going to get - One of <i>their</i> people has been targeted by a vampire.<br /> <br /> From the vampires point of view, there's no real easy way to differentiate these from their regular prey. And I think few vampires would be willing to constrain their feeding to avoid someone who <i>might</i> be related to a werewolf pack. Placing further restrictions within their feeding grounds is a big deal.<br /> <br /> With sufficient numbers of each, conflict seems pretty inevitable. And avoiding it seems like a lot of sacrifice that neither side will be willing to make. If they're balanced in power, I think you'll see a lot of conflict. If the werewolves are dominant, I'd expect to see more vampires within packs and the freelancers being very careful about who they feed on. If the vampires are dominant, they're going to feed on whoever they want. I don't know if the werewolves have a good reaction to that short of escalating to outright war.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering Vampires tend towards large cities with millions of inhabitants, I think your overestimating the overlap of 30-40 people, let alone realizing someone was even fed on or otherwise influenced without constantly controlling and watching your extended pack like a sheep dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T16:30:32-07:00","id":857333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/850497-2e-feeding-on-werewolves?p=857243#post857243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With sufficient numbers of each, conflict seems pretty inevitable. And avoiding it seems like a lot of sacrifice that neither side will be willing to make. If they're balanced in power, I think you'll see a lot of conflict. If the werewolves are dominant, I'd expect to see more vampires within packs and the freelancers being very careful about who they feed on. If the vampires are dominant, they're going to feed on whoever they want. I don't know if the werewolves have a good reaction to that short of escalating to outright war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since they don't actually compete for territory and since, like in 1e, they want different things I don't really see how conflict is inevitable, except maybe among violent young hotheads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T18:05:51-07:00","id":857373,"title":"","content":"And werewolves have a lot of ways to easily locate vampires. Especially within their territory. If there was going to be a conflict, the werewolves could feel the vampire out before it could become an actual problem. Since most vampires have, basically, steady feeding sources, it becomes a matter of telling the pack not to go to that bar, or the vampire not to feed off the Jefferson family.<br /> <br /> Either way, if a werewolf did decide to kill a vampire, or vampires managed to kill an entire pack, it's not likely the kind of thing that would lead to a war, mainly because vampires aren't exactly a unified front and unless the pack is part of a protectorate there's no guarantee anyone else would care. Even if there was a protectorate.<br /> <br /> But that's just possibilities. I'm not trying to be the verisimilitude police and there's plenty of ways to set it up in your game so that things work the way you want. But, books as given, don't really have a werewolf versus vampire antagonism built in to it.<br /> <br /> I believe the developer said it well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#3E3E3E\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">An MI6 agent observes a CIA man in 1974 Moscow. She knows what he is \u2014 she can tell by the newspapers he reads, by the routes he drives and what brands of cigarettes he buys on what days. She doesn't need to ask him, and he doesn't need to ask her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3E3E3E\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Every month or so, they meet in a park; mostly, they exchange pleasantries and empty platitudes. Sometimes they share information \u2014 or disinformation \u2014 but broadly, they both have the same goal. She may set a bomb under a junior minister's car; he may spend a night with a senior security guard, turning him into a double agent. Their methods are different, but they both want the same thing in the end. They come from different places, but you can recognize them by their similarities as much as their differences.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#3E3E3E\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">But, again, the game has the tools to put the setting you want for your game together. Seeing 'Garou' made me think people were thinking Forsaken was more like Apocalypse, with the wyrm-taint hate.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-01-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}